.TH cpp 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
cpp \- the C preprocessor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpp
[\fB\-D\fIname\fR[\fB=\fIvalue\fR]] [\fB\-I\fIdir\fR] [\fIinput\fR [\fIoutput\fR]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cpp
expands the
.BR #include ,
.BR #define ,
.B #if
family and macro calls, and writes the result.
.BR cc (1)
runs it for you;
.B cpp
by hand, or
.BR "cc \-E" ,
is for finding out what a macro actually expands to.
.SH NOTES
This is the board's own preprocessor, not
.BR "gcc \-E" .
A cross-compiled build uses gcc, so anything that works there is not
evidence that it works here.  C89 is what to expect.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cc (1)
